infographic compare-swot
data
  title The write-path trilemma: each strategy sacrifices one of fast, fresh, durable
  desc Three write strategies, three different promises kept — and one broken
  compares
    - label Write-through
      children
        - label Keeps: freshness
          desc Cache and DB written synchronously — never stale on writes
        - label Sacrifices: write latency
          desc Two synchronous trips per write; pair with a TTL to evict cache churn
    - label Write-back
      children
        - label Keeps: write latency
          desc Cache written now, DB flushed async — lowest latency, coalesces bursts
        - label Sacrifices: durability
          desc Un-flushed writes are lost if the cache node dies — fits counters, not money
    - label Write-around
      children
        - label Keeps: no cache churn
          desc Writes only the DB, so write-heavy data never pollutes the cache
        - label Sacrifices: first-read freshness
          desc Guaranteed miss on the first read after a write; value enters lazily
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e #14b8a6
